{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"454587","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/454587","key":"MC-296431","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"08/Apr/25 2:06 PM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>If one makes a resource pack and intends to hide the slot like below, clipping the item to a 16x16 slot is not viable. Additionally, if you were to have an item larger than the specific 16x16 space, it causes visual errors in items in your inventory (as shown below), we could have it clip to just enough (1.125x item model scale) to allow this feature and keep the clipping ability, though it would need space around each item lest you get it flowing into other items.</p>\n\n<p>Steps to reproduce:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Open using the recent snapshot</li>\n\t<li>Download and mount the resource pack</li>\n\t<li>Copy in the an item from the following code, other options for the custom model data string are: <tt>empty</tt>,<tt>right_arrow</tt>, <tt>left_arrow</tt>, <tt>cross</tt>, <tt>left_arrow_disabled</tt>, <tt>right_arrow_disabled</tt></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>/give @s stick[\n  minecraft:item_model=\"minecraft:gui_button\",\n  minecraft:item_name={\"text\":\"Back\"},\n  minecraft:custom_model_data={\n    strings:[\"minecraft:left_arrow\"],\n    flags:[true]\n  }\n]</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>observe the item you receive does not cover the borders as it was designed to and previously used to.</li>\n\t<li>observe that some items in your inventory might just vanish.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>Try again on 1.21.5 and notice it works as expected.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":null,"cus